# CoreOS needs one AI provider configured. Pick whichever you can pay for —
# the agents behave the same either way.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development, or set the variables in
# your hosting provider's environment settings.
#
# Without either, the app still runs: every agent returns a clearly-labelled
# message saying no key is configured, instead of a real answer.

# --- Option 1: Anthropic direct (preferred; wins if both are set) -----------
# Runs Claude Haiku 4.5, which the agent personas are tuned against.
# Keys: https://console.anthropic.com  (pay-as-you-go; there is no free tier)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Option 2: OpenRouter ---------------------------------------------------
# One key across many providers, including models that are free to call.
# Keys:   https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Models: https://openrouter.ai/models  — anything ending ":free" costs nothing
#
# Both variables are required. OPENROUTER_MODEL has no default on purpose:
# model ids on aggregators get renamed and retired, and a stale hardcoded one
# fails as "model not found" rather than anything that points at the cause.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# Optional. Sent as the attribution header on OpenRouter calls.
OPENROUTER_SITE_URL=
